Class C of the PR #244 failure set: version-gates (windows-latest), step
"Test component-path-diff-basis suite (pwsh)", GitHub Actions run
31755520663 / job 94630322035.

Defect: tests/component-path-diff-basis.tests.ps1 created the TEST-021 fixture
"src/desktop/tab<TAB>name.ts" on disk. Win32 reserves 0x00-0x1F in a path
component, so Set-Content throws "The filename, directory name, or volume
label syntax is incorrect."; under this file's $ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"
that terminated the whole suite at TEST-021, and TEST-022..TEST-025,
DEFECT-002 and the registration self-check were never reached.

Distinct from Class A (78d79cd5, TEST-024 cloned-submodule git identity, the
ubuntu leg). The windows leg fails earlier and for an unrelated filesystem
reason.

Host for every run below: macOS (darwin 25.5.0), PowerShell 7.6.2, APFS.
APFS accepts TAB in a filename, so the windows-latest condition is reproduced
by mutation rather than by platform: a disposable copy of the suite whose
Set-Content call site is replaced by a throw carrying Win32's own message.
Only that one line differs from the committed suite; the skip branch and
TEST-021.3 below run for real.

===========================================================================
0. MECHANISM CONFIRMED FIRST (pre-fix behaviour, isolated)
===========================================================================
An unhandled Set-Content failure under $ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"
terminates the script rather than producing a FAIL line:

    $ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"
    Write-Output "before"
    "x" | Set-Content -LiteralPath "/nonexistent-dir-xyz/tab`tname.ts" -Encoding utf8
    Write-Output "after"

  -> prints "before", the Set-Content error, exit 1. "after" never printed.

That is the CI symptom: everything after the failing line is lost.

