Note: this mutation is what caught a defect in TEST-021.3's own first
draft. Splitting the token makes the NEXT token be read as a status word,
so the real Get-TrackedDiff THROWS rather than returning a wrong value.
With no catch, that throw escaped and killed the suite (exit 1, no FAIL
line, TEST-022..025 lost) -- reintroducing the exact failure mode this
change removes. TEST-021.3 now catches it and reports a FAIL, and the
run above reaches the registration self-check.

