===========================================================================
6. SCOPE, STATED HONESTLY
===========================================================================
Not verified here: a real windows-latest runner. No Windows host was
available, so the NTFS rejection is reproduced by mutation (section 2)
rather than observed. What sections 2-4 do establish is that WHEN the
filesystem refuses the name, the suite runs to completion, says so in
its output, and still asserts AC-021's TAB round-trip against the real
parsing functions -- and that the substitute assertion fails on both a
framing regression and a decode regression. Whether windows-latest takes
that branch at all can only be confirmed by a real CI cycle.

Also not covered by TEST-021.3, and stated rather than implied: that git
itself emits such a path NUL-delimited under -z. Only TEST-021.1's
end-to-end fixture covers that, which is why it stays preferred on every
host whose filesystem can hold the name.
